  "pli-tv-bu-vb-sk36:1.3.1": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Sūpa</i> is defined at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/pli-tv-bu-vb-sk29/en/brahmali#1.4.1'>Bu Sk 29:1.4.1</a> as bean curry. <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Byañjana</i> is explained at Khuddasikkhā-abhinavaṭīkā, para. 61 as <i lang='pi' translate='no'>macchamaṁsādibyañjanañca</i>, “And <i lang='pi' translate='no'>byañjana</i> of fish, meat, etc.” So <i lang='pi' translate='no'>byañjana</i> seems to refer to fine curries, whereas <i lang='pi' translate='no'>sūpa</i> is more ordinary. ",
